def lists_to_nested_dict(keys, values):
    if len(keys)!= len(values):
        raise ValueError("Keys and values lists must be of the same length")

    result = {}
    for key, value in zip(keys, values):
        result[key] = value if isinstance(value, dict) else {key: value}
        if isinstance(result[key], dict):
            result[key] = lists_to_nested_dict(list(result[key].keys()), list(result[key].values()))

    return result
```

This function assumes that the keys and values lists are of the same length and that each key corresponds to a single value. It recursively processes nested dictionaries within the resulting dictionary.

